/* The 97k theme's character-select name tags (CCharInfoBalloonMng), as the 0.97k client wrote them
   over each character (Scene_CharSelect.cpp): no balloon art and no guild line, just the name in
   the bold font over the class and level ("Dark Knight 150"), each line centred on its own
   half-black band as wide as its text. The name is the 0.97k client's light blue (0xffffc8b4); a
   flagged character's name is black on a coloured band instead: yellow for a blocked character,
   cyan for blocked items, blue for an operator. The class line is white.
   C++ places the foot of Sven's 118x54 tag box at the point the 0.97k client projected, 190
   over the character's feet. That client wrote the class line from that point down and the name
   above it; here both stand 3 pixels higher (top 51px instead of 54px). Both lines take the font
   size set in the options, whatever the window's size, and the name stands its height plus 3 higher
   on the 640x480 screen (#balloons' font-size and --classic-name-rise, set by C++). The tags are
   hidden while the character-creation dialog is open, as the 0.97k client hid them. */

#balloons.char-make-open {
	display: none;
}

.balloon {
	position: absolute;
	width: 118px;
	height: 54px;
	pointer-events: none;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}
.balloon-bg, .balloon-guild {
	display: none;
}

.balloon-name, .balloon-class {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	transform: translateX(-50%);
	padding: 0 2px;
	white-space: nowrap;
	line-height: 1;
	background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 128);
}
.balloon-name {
	top: calc(51px - var(--classic-name-rise));
	font-weight: bold;
	color: #b4c8ff;
}
.balloon-class {
	top: 51px;
	color: #ffffff;
}

.balloon-name.name-blocked-character { color: #000000; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 0, 128); }
.balloon-name.name-blocked-items     { color: #000000; background-color: rgba(0, 255, 255, 128); }
.balloon-name.name-operator          { color: #000000; background-color: rgba(0, 0, 255, 128); }
